[{"text": "I now give the floor to his excellency", "start": 2.0, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "George Shatula Shapunda, Minister for", "start": 4.24, "duration": 7.08}, {"text": "Foreign Affairs of Malawi.", "start": 6.799, "duration": 4.521}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 32.399, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "your excellencies,", "start": 35.28, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "distinguished delegates,", "start": 37.84, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "I have the honor and privilege to", "start": 40.32, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "deliver this statement", "start": 42.16, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "on behalf of his excellency,", "start": 44.879, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Professor Arthur Peter,", "start": 47.52, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "President of the Republic of Malawi and", "start": 50.079, "duration": 6.361}, {"text": "the people of Malawi.", "start": 52.879, "duration": 3.561}, {"text": "I congratulate you, Mr. President and", "start": 58.32, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "all vice presidents on your election to", "start": 60.64, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "lead this at one session of the United", "start": 63.68, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "Nations General Assembly.", "start": 66.96, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "Malawi pledges his full support your", "start": 71.36, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "leadership. We also extend our profound", "start": 73.68, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "appreciation to the secretary general", "start": 76.799, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "for his unwavering dedication to our", "start": 79.28, "duration": 6.199}, {"text": "shared global values.", "start": 81.6, "duration": 3.879}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 85.84, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "the theme for this session,", "start": 88.159, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "restoring trust, managing", "start": 91.2, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "transformation,", "start": 93.2, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "a united nation that delivers for all,", "start": 94.72, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "strikes at the heart of our current", "start": 99.2, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "global reality.", "start": 101.2, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "We live in an era of deep fractures.", "start": 104.72, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "Trust between nations has eroded. Global", "start": 108.32, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "systems are failing to manage rapid", "start": 111.92, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "technological, economic, and", "start": 114.0, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "environmental shifts equitably.", "start": 116.24, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "For the United Nation to remain", "start": 119.04, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "relevant,", "start": 120.799, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "it must transform into an institution", "start": 123.6, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "that delivers tangible progress for the", "start": 125.68, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "most vulnerable,", "start": 128.56, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "leaving no nation behind. I would", "start": 130.479, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "therefore like to highlight six", "start": 133.44, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "opportunities", "start": 136.4, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "for restoring trust, managing", "start": 137.92, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "transformation and thereby ensuring a", "start": 140.879, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "united nations", "start": 144.0, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "that delivers for all.", "start": 146.16, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "The first opportunities are celebrating", "start": 149.36, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "sustainable development and economic", "start": 152.16, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "transformation.", "start": 154.959, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "Mr. President, the timeline for the 2030", "start": 157.76, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "agenda for sustainable development is", "start": 161.44, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "rapidly drawing to a close.", "start": 164.4, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "Yet the promise", "start": 167.36, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "of the sustainable development goals", "start": 170.239, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "remain dangerously out of reach for", "start": 172.56, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "millions.", "start": 175.44, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "For Malawi, the pursuit of wealth", "start": 178.239, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "creation, self-reliance, and economic", "start": 180.48, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "transformation is not merely a political", "start": 183.28, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "aspiration. It is an urgent survival", "start": 185.36, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "strategy.", "start": 188.8, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Because of this, we have remained", "start": 192.4, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "steadfast in implementing the SDGs in", "start": 194.64, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "alignment with our long-term development", "start": 198.4, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "vision, the Malawi 2063.", "start": 200.56, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "On this note, Mr. President, I'm happy", "start": 204.239, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "to report that Malawi", "start": 206.959, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "successfully", "start": 209.44, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "presented our third voluntary national", "start": 210.959, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "review during the 2026 Echoso High Level", "start": 213.36, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "Political Forum, thereby reaffirming our", "start": 217.28, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "commitment to the 2030 agenda for", "start": 220.4, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "sustainable development and the Malawi", "start": 223.12, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "2063", "start": 226.64, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "as well as our desire to accelerate", "start": 228.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "sustainable development and economic", "start": 231.04, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "transformation.", "start": 233.68, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "The review revealed that even though we", "start": 235.84, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "face numerous structural challenges, we", "start": 238.239, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "have made some progress on many of the", "start": 241.04, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "SDGs.", "start": 243.04, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "Mr. President, our goal is to", "start": 246.0, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "systematically transform our economy by", "start": 248.239, "duration": 6.28}, {"text": "modernizing agriculture,", "start": 250.72, "duration": 3.799}, {"text": "expanding mining, and accelerating", "start": 255.12, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "digitalization.", "start": 258.32, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "However, national efforts alone cannot", "start": 259.919, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "dismantle the structural barriers built", "start": 263.04, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "into the global economic architecture.", "start": 265.52, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "Developing nations require deliberate", "start": 269.68, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "scaled investment in industrialization,", "start": 272.16, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "sustainable infrastructure and regional", "start": 275.199, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "value chains to transition from primary", "start": 277.919, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "commodity exporters to diversified", "start": 281.44, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "industrialized", "start": 284.72, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "economies.", "start": 286.56, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "In addition, we cannot achieve", "start": 288.72, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "sustainable development while drowning", "start": 290.479, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "in debt. Malawi therefore calls for", "start": 292.96, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "immediate comprehensive debt relief and", "start": 296.32, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "restructuring.", "start": 299.28, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "The current international financial", "start": 300.8, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "architecture forces developing nation to", "start": 303.84, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "choose", "start": 306.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "between servicing", "start": 309.199, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "predatory deaths and investing in", "start": 311.44, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "health, education and climate", "start": 313.68, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "resilience.", "start": 315.68, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "This is a moral failure. Mr. President,", "start": 317.84, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "we also call for a massive scaling up of", "start": 322.08, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "concessional development financing.", "start": 324.56, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "We need targeted investment in our key", "start": 328.56, "duration": 6.639}, {"text": "productive sectors, namely agriculture,", "start": 331.039, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "industrialization and infrastructure", "start": 335.199, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "development as follows.", "start": 338.0, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "agriculture modernization through", "start": 341.28, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "mechanization and commercialization to", "start": 343.44, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "guarantee food security.", "start": 346.479, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "Second, building local industry so that", "start": 349.36, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "we stop exporting raw materials and", "start": 352.16, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "create decent job for our youth who make", "start": 354.639, "duration": 7.361}, {"text": "up nearly 40% of the Malawi population.", "start": 357.6, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "And thirdly, developing robust", "start": 362.0, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "transport, energy, and digital", "start": 364.88, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "infrastructure to connect Malawi to", "start": 366.96, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "regional and global market.", "start": 369.759, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "We therefore call upon our international", "start": 372.24, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "partners to align their support with", "start": 374.56, "duration": 6.639}, {"text": "national blueprint like the Malawi 2063", "start": 377.6, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "in order to generate meaningful job", "start": 381.199, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "creation and shared prosperity.", "start": 383.36, "duration": 4.839}, {"text": "The second opportunity is strengthening", "start": 388.24, "duration": 6.04}, {"text": "climate action resilient.", "start": 390.319, "duration": 3.961}, {"text": "Mr. President, Malawi contributes", "start": 394.319, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "negligibly to global greenhouse gas", "start": 397.039, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "emissions. Yet, we remain on the front", "start": 399.68, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "line of the climate crisis. In recent", "start": 402.319, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "years, devastating cyclones, prolonged", "start": 405.199, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "droughts, and increasingly erratic", "start": 408.24, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "weather patterns have destroyed", "start": 410.24, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "infrastructure,", "start": 412.72, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "devastated crops, displaced thousands of", "start": 414.72, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "our seasoned and inflicted severe damage", "start": 418.4, "duration": 5.799}, {"text": "on our economy.", "start": 420.639, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "This year we face the added threat of El", "start": 424.56, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "Nuno related extreme weather which risks", "start": 426.8, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "further undermining livelihood, food", "start": 429.599, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "security and economic stability. As such", "start": 432.72, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "we are fighting back by embedding", "start": 436.479, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "climate resilience into our national", "start": 439.12, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "development planning and strengthening", "start": 441.199, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "locally locally driven adaptation", "start": 443.84, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "measures.", "start": 447.12, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "However, our efforts are continually", "start": 449.919, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "outpaced by the scale and speed of", "start": 452.479, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "climate change. Climate shocks", "start": 455.12, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "repeatedly destroy infrastructure,", "start": 457.52, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "decimate", "start": 460.4, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "agriculture production,", "start": 462.319, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "and make worse food insecurity and erode", "start": 464.72, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "hard development gains.", "start": 467.52, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "Mr. President, the global community must", "start": 470.72, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "therefore move beyond rhetoric and", "start": 473.919, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "translate commitments into meaningful", "start": 476.72, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "action. We call for the full and", "start": 478.96, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "effective operationalization", "start": 482.24, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "and capitalization of the loss and", "start": 484.72, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "damage fund.", "start": 487.36, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "Major historical and current emitters", "start": 489.28, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "must honor their climate finance", "start": 491.919, "duration": 3.601}, {"text": "commitments", "start": 494.0, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "by providing accessible,", "start": 495.52, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "predictable, grant-based and highly", "start": 498.96, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "concessionable financing rather than", "start": 501.68, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "relying on debt creating instrument that", "start": 504.24, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "further burden vulnerable countries", "start": 506.639, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "already struggling to cope with the", "start": 509.44, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "consequences of a crisis. They did not", "start": 511.68, "duration": 7.039}, {"text": "little they did little to cause.", "start": 513.76, "duration": 7.279}, {"text": "Mr. President, Malawi therefore calls", "start": 518.719, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "for enhanced, predictable and easily", "start": 521.039, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "accessible climate finance with greater", "start": 524.08, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "emphasis on adaptation and disaster risk", "start": 526.959, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "reduction.", "start": 530.32, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "We need sustainable investment in early", "start": 533.279, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "air warning systems, climate resilience", "start": 536.0, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "infrastructure, sustainable land", "start": 538.959, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "management, climate smart agriculture", "start": 541.279, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "and locally laid adaptation.", "start": 543.839, "duration": 6.881}, {"text": "Climate change is an existential threat", "start": 547.839, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "to Malawi's development and to the hard", "start": 550.72, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "one gains we have made.", "start": 553.519, "duration": 6.561}, {"text": "Mr. President the third opportunities to", "start": 556.48, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "reform global governance and", "start": 560.08, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "strengthening multilateralism.", "start": 561.76, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "The current global challenges underscore", "start": 566.24, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "a fundamental truth.", "start": 568.32, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "Our multilateral framework is fractured", "start": 571.04, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "because its foundational architecture is", "start": 574.56, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "obsolete. The institution designed in", "start": 577.12, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "1945 no longer reflects the geopolitical", "start": 579.92, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "and economic realities of 2026.", "start": 583.519, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "Malai will reaffirm this unwavering", "start": 586.88, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "commitment to multilateralism but it", "start": 589.2, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "must be a multilateralism that is", "start": 591.839, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "inclusive, fair and democratic.", "start": 593.839, "duration": 6.881}, {"text": "We call for an urgent comprehensive", "start": 598.48, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "reform of the United Nations Security", "start": 600.72, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Council to correct the historical", "start": 602.72, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "injustice done to Africa. Africa", "start": 605.04, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "deserves", "start": 607.839, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "payment representation with full veto", "start": 609.839, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "privileges at articulation in the", "start": 612.399, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "concessors.", "start": 616.0, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "Furthermore, the international financing", "start": 617.519, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "architecture specifically the IMF and", "start": 620.399, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "the world bank must be radically", "start": 622.72, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "overhauled.", "start": 624.56, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "The current system traps developing", "start": 627.519, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "nation in cycles of unsustainable debt,", "start": 629.92, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "forcing government to choose between", "start": 633.839, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "servicing foreign loans or funding basic", "start": 636.48, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "education and health care for their", "start": 639.76, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "citizens.", "start": 641.76, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Mr. President because Malawi strongly", "start": 643.68, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "believe in multilateralism. We take", "start": 646.0, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "responsibility when called upon by the", "start": 648.56, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "international community to participate", "start": 650.64, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "in causes that further the aims of this", "start": 652.88, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "organization. Malawi remains firmly", "start": 655.92, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "committed to the rule of law,", "start": 658.8, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "accountability and the peaceful", "start": 660.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "resolution of dispute as indispensable", "start": 662.32, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "foundation of an effective materal", "start": 665.68, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "system.", "start": 668.399, "duration": 3.601}, {"text": "It is in this spirit that Malawi has", "start": 669.92, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "presented the candidature of lady", "start": 672.0, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "justice to Galani Chisumir for election", "start": 673.92, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "of as a judge of the international", "start": 677.44, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "criminal court for the term 2027 to 20", "start": 679.519, "duration": 7.401}, {"text": "2036.", "start": 683.92, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Justice Jizil is a distinguished jurist", "start": 687.76, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "with extensive judicial and legal", "start": 691.76, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "experience at the national,", "start": 695.2, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "regional and international levels,", "start": 698.56, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "including her service as a judge of the", "start": 701.44, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "African court on human and people's", "start": 703.92, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "rights. Her candidate reflects Malawi", "start": 706.079, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "commitment to strengthening", "start": 709.279, "duration": 3.201}, {"text": "international justice through", "start": 710.56, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "experienced, independent, and highly", "start": 712.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "qualified judicial leadership.", "start": 714.48, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "As state test parties prepare to elect", "start": 717.2, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "six judges to the international criminal", "start": 719.68, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "court in December 2026,", "start": 721.76, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "Malawi respectively seeks the values", "start": 724.399, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "support", "start": 726.88, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "of state parties for the candidature of", "start": 728.48, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "lady justice.", "start": 731.6, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "We are confident that her extensive", "start": 734.88, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "judicial experience, commitment to the", "start": 736.959, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "rule of law and demonstrated service to", "start": 739.44, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "justice and human rights would enable", "start": 742.399, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "her to make a meaningful contribution to", "start": 744.32, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "the work of the court. Malawi looks", "start": 746.959, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "forward to the support of fellow states", "start": 749.68, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "parties for her election and to", "start": 752.48, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "continuing our collective efforts to", "start": 754.88, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "strengthen the institutions of", "start": 757.36, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "international justice.", "start": 759.04, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "Mr. President, the fourth opportunity", "start": 763.04, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "for restoring trust, managing", "start": 765.12, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "transformation, and thereby ensuring a", "start": 767.839, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "united nation that delivers for all lies", "start": 770.959, "duration": 8.281}, {"text": "in strengthening global health security.", "start": 774.399, "duration": 4.841}, {"text": "Economic transformation and sustainable", "start": 780.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "development are impossible without a", "start": 782.959, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "healthy population. The vulnerabilities", "start": 785.68, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "exposed by recent global pandemics", "start": 788.8, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "continue to linger, reminding us that", "start": 791.279, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "global health security is only as strong", "start": 793.839, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "as it weakest link. Malawi is making", "start": 797.04, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "strides towards achieving", "start": 799.92, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "universal health coverage and", "start": 802.72, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "strengthening our primary health care", "start": 805.04, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "system.", "start": 806.959, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "However, systematic", "start": 809.2, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "systemic global inequities in health", "start": 812.16, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "care access, medical manufacturing and", "start": 815.36, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "vaccine distribution remain glaringly", "start": 818.24, "duration": 7.88}, {"text": "unresolved.", "start": 823.12, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "True global health security demands", "start": 826.48, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "decentralized pharmaceutical", "start": 829.12, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "manufacturing capabilities and", "start": 831.279, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "restricted technology transfer and", "start": 833.92, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "intellectual property", "start": 836.959, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "waver during health emergencies.", "start": 839.76, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "My de delegation appeals to all of us", "start": 842.72, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "here to finalize a robust legally", "start": 845.36, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "binding pandemic treaty that guarantees", "start": 847.6, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "equity, solidarity, and immediate", "start": 850.88, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "resource sharing for the global south.", "start": 853.68, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "We also call for collaboration in", "start": 858.24, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "efforts to build long-term resilience", "start": 860.24, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "against pandemics through investment in", "start": 863.199, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "our domestic pharmaceutical", "start": 865.68, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "manufacturing capacity by producing", "start": 867.839, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "essential medicine within Africa. The", "start": 870.959, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "entire world gain through stronger", "start": 873.44, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "health security and stable supply chain", "start": 875.279, "duration": 8.401}, {"text": "especially through faster outbreak", "start": 880.959, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "response.", "start": 883.68, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "Mr. President the fifth opportunities to", "start": 885.6, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "promote human rights, peace and", "start": 888.48, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "international security. Malawi firmly", "start": 891.519, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "believe that development, peace and", "start": 894.72, "duration": 6.559}, {"text": "human rights as in extremely linked. We", "start": 897.04, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "remain deeply committed to upholding the", "start": 901.279, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "constitutional rights of all our citizen", "start": 903.519, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "strengthening our democratic institution", "start": 906.16, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "and maintaining an uncompromising stance", "start": 908.48, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "against corruption. Furthermore, we", "start": 911.12, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "strongly defend the right to development", "start": 913.6, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "as an ineliable human right. True", "start": 916.24, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "freedom cannot exist in condition of", "start": 919.76, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "extreme poverty and systemic economic", "start": 922.16, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "exclusion.", "start": 925.76, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "On the global stage, we view with great", "start": 927.279, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "alarm the proliferation of violent", "start": 930.16, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "conflicts and constitutional changes of", "start": 932.399, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "government, geopolitical fragmentation", "start": 935.04, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "and acts of racism, racial", "start": 937.6, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "discrimination, xenophobia and related", "start": 939.92, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "intolerance. Mr. President, the Malawi", "start": 942.48, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "nation is not standing alone. As all", "start": 945.36, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "these alarming developments are come,", "start": 948.399, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "Malai will continue to play part in", "start": 950.24, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "global peace operation, deploying our", "start": 952.399, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "brave men and women to United Nations", "start": 954.88, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "peacekeeping mission to safeguard", "start": 957.519, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "stability on our continent. In this", "start": 959.36, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "regard, let me reiterate the calls for", "start": 962.079, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "immediate secession of hostilities in", "start": 964.32, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "all active conflict zones worldwide.", "start": 966.72, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "Global resource currently being funneled", "start": 969.6, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "into destructive warfare should instead", "start": 972.079, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "be redirected towards eradicating", "start": 974.72, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "poverty, building schools, and financing", "start": 978.0, "duration": 6.519}, {"text": "sustainable development.", "start": 980.88, "duration": 3.639}, {"text": "We also reaffirm our solidarity with", "start": 984.56, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "global efforts to combat racism, racial", "start": 987.04, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "discrimination, xenophobia, and related", "start": 989.839, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "intolerance.", "start": 992.56, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "Mr. President, as we take steps to grab", "start": 994.32, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "these opportunities, we must also", "start": 996.72, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "recognize the emergence of artificial", "start": 999.279, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "intelligence which presents both", "start": 1001.44, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "opportunities and threats to humanity.", "start": 1003.6, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "Malai, we welcome the transformative", "start": 1006.399, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "potential for AI as an expression of", "start": 1008.48, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "human ingenuity and as an increasingly", "start": 1011.6, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "important tool for accelerating", "start": 1014.639, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "sustainable development for developing", "start": 1016.639, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "countries including Malawi. AI offers", "start": 1019.279, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "opportunities to strengthen agricultural", "start": 1022.16, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "productivity and food security, improve", "start": 1024.48, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "health care and education, enhance", "start": 1027.52, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "climate resilient and disaster", "start": 1029.839, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "preparedness, expand financial inclusion", "start": 1031.76, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "and improve the efficiency of public", "start": 1034.559, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "service. Malawi believes however that", "start": 1037.12, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "technological advancements must remain", "start": 1039.679, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "human centered.", "start": 1042.0, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "Artificial intelligence should", "start": 1044.079, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "complement and enhance human", "start": 1045.52, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "capabilities rather than diminish the", "start": 1047.439, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "indispensable role of people in shaping", "start": 1049.919, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "their own development.", "start": 1052.64, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "At the same time, Malawi will recognize", "start": 1055.84, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "that the rapid expansion of artificial", "start": 1057.52, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "intelligence presents significant", "start": 1059.679, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "challenges particularly for developing", "start": 1061.6, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "economy with fragile labor markets and", "start": 1063.919, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "limited technological infrastructure.", "start": 1066.799, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "Automation could disrupt employment and", "start": 1069.679, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "widen existing inequalities while an", "start": 1072.08, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "equal access to computing cap capacity,", "start": 1074.88, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "data, digital infrastructure, skills and", "start": 1078.799, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "financing risk creating a new", "start": 1081.2, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "technological divide between and within", "start": 1085.039, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "countries. Malai therefore calls upon", "start": 1087.919, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "the United Nation to continue promoting", "start": 1090.48, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "an inclusive, ethical and", "start": 1093.2, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "developmentoriented global framework for", "start": 1095.76, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "AI governance. One that safeguards human", "start": 1098.24, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "dignity and employment. Builds the", "start": 1101.44, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "technological capacities of developing", "start": 1103.919, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "countries. facilitate equitable access", "start": 1106.16, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "to AI technologies and ensure that the", "start": 1109.12, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "benefits of innovation", "start": 1113.2, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "contribute directly to the achievement", "start": 1115.44, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "of the sustainable development goals. No", "start": 1117.2, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "country should be left behind in the", "start": 1120.48, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "emerging AIdriven global economy. Mr.", "start": 1122.88, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "President, in conclusion,", "start": 1127.2, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "restoring trust requires honesty,", "start": 1130.08, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "accountability, and action. Managing", "start": 1132.559, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "transformation requires courage, vision,", "start": 1135.679, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "and solidarity.", "start": 1138.4, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "The choices we make today will", "start": 1140.32, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "reverberate for generation to come. We", "start": 1142.08, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "can choose to retreat into isolationism", "start": 1144.96, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "and protectionism or we can choose to", "start": 1147.28, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "summon the political courage required to", "start": 1149.76, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "build a fairer, more resilient and", "start": 1152.24, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "inclusive world. Malawi stands ready to", "start": 1154.32, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "play part. We are transforming our", "start": 1157.2, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "economy, reforming our institution and", "start": 1159.6, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "investing in our people. But we cannot", "start": 1162.48, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "do it alone in an unfair global", "start": 1164.88, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "environment. We stand ready to work hand", "start": 1167.44, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "in hand with all member states to bridge", "start": 1169.679, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "the divise, restore trust in", "start": 1172.24, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "multilateralism and deliver a", "start": 1175.28, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "sustainable dignified future for all", "start": 1177.28, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "humanity. Let this first session of the", "start": 1179.36, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "general assembly mark the turning point", "start": 1183.44, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "where the United Nation transitions from", "start": 1187.2, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "a forum of speeches to an engine of", "start": 1189.919, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "delivery. Let us build a united nation", "start": 1192.4, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "that delivers wealth instead of poverty,", "start": 1195.28, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "resilience instead of vulnerability", "start": 1198.96, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "and peace instead of conflict. A United", "start": 1201.76, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "Nation that delivers for all. Thank you", "start": 1205.12, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "very much for your attention.", "start": 1208.32, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "I thank the Minister for Foreign Affairs", "start": 1216.64, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "of Malawi.", "start": 1218.88, "duration": 3.4}]